<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Westphalia</h1><p class="st-meta">1807 CE – 1813 CE · capital Kassel</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Napoleonic kingdom ruled by his brother Jérôme, Germany's first state with a written constitution and equal rights for Jews.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> created the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a> in 1807 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaties-of-tilsit">Peace of Tilsit</a>, combining <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/electorate-of-hesse">Hesse-Kassel</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-wolfenbuttel">Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel</a>, Prussian lands west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halberstadt">Halberstadt</a>, and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>. He gave it to his youngest brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerome-bonaparte">Jérôme Bonaparte</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a> as capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The constitution of November 1807, the first in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfdom">serfdom</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guild</a> privileges, introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-code">Napoleonic Code</a> and granted equal rights to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>. A parliament of estates met. But heavy taxes, French demands for soldiers and losses in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> made the regime unpopular, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerome-bonaparte">Jérôme</a>'s court was known for extravagance. Revolts broke out in 1809.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a> in 1813 Russian troops took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerome-bonaparte">Jérôme</a> fled. The old rulers returned to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/electorate-of-hesse">Hesse-Kassel</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> recovered its lands.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-westphalia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Westphalia" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: Maxek 2005 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kingdom_of_Westphalia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1807 CE – 1813 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kassel</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jérôme Bonaparte</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism, Calvinism, Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Königreich Westphalen</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=kingdom-of-westphalia" aria-label="Kingdom of Westphalia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4895 400 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Westphalia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5215 656L5243 641M5215 656L5262 633M5215 656L5215 656M5215 656L5193 634M5215 656L5237 632M5215 656L5219 626M5215 656L5190 642M5215 656L5200 629M5215 656L5249 640M5215 656L5054 728M5215 656L5199 691"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5243 641h0M5262 633h0M5215 656h0M5193 634h0M5237 632h0M5219 626h0M5190 642h0M5200 629h0M5249 640h0M5054 728h0M5199 691h0"/><p